messages:
Aisha (Docs): Heads up — noticed our structured output page still links to the old anchor /tool-calling#json-output :eyes: I opened a tiny PR to fix the anchors and add a compatibility note. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/489
Omar (SDK): Nice, can you also include a TypeScript SDK snippet showing the new response envelope + a robust parse example (with fallback for null arrays)?
Benjamin (Eng-ML): We see a lot of clients failing when model returns \"tools\": null instead of an empty array. Quick shim suggestion: 
```
const tools = resp.tools || [];
// safe to map over tools now
```
That would solve a bunch of support tickets.
Aisha (Docs): Good call. I'll add that shim and a short migration blurb under "Compatibility notes". Also will grep for changed anchors.
Kei (Eng-Runtime): FYI runtime will default to returning empty arrays for v2 models next week, but docs need to cover older responses too. cc @Benjamin
Automations (deploy-bot): Preview build ready: https://deploy-preview-489--docs.redwood.ai/structured-output (expires in 48h) :building_construction:
Omar (SDK): Also suggest we include a small JSON Schema guardrail example so readers can validate responses before parsing. Example: 
```js
const schema = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    tools: { type: ['array', 'null'], items: { type: 'object' } }
  },
  required: ['tools']
};
validate(resp, schema);
```
Aisha (Docs): Perfect. I'll add both the shim and the schema snippet. Planning to update the TS and Python SDK snippets under /sdk-snippets too.
Benjamin (Eng-ML): If possible, add one tiny unit test in the docs repo that runs the snippet with `tools = null` and asserts no exception — helps catch regressions.
Aisha (Docs): Good idea — I'll add a test under docs/tests/snippets/test_parse_null_tools.js in the PR. Targeting to merge by EOD PST. @Kei can you confirm there won't be a runtime rollback that would break the preview?
Kei (Eng-Runtime): No rollback planned. Safe to merge.
Omar (SDK): LGTM once the examples are in. Thanks Aisha! :thumbsup:
Aisha (Docs): Thanks everyone — I'll follow up in the PR thread with the exact file list I changed and a short changelog entry for the release notes.
